  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Inside the parentheses, \\(1-\\frac{1}{x+1}=\\frac{x}{x+1}\\). Dividing by \\(\\frac{x}{x^2-1}\\) means multiplying by \\(\\frac{x^2-1}{x}\\), giving \\((x-1)\\). When \\(x=5\\), its value is \\(4\\).",
